For all layers _m_ **d**<sup>_m_</sup> \\uf028\\uf029 _t_ = \\uf0e5 \\uf05b **S**<sup>_u_</sup> \\uf02c<sup>_m_</sup> \\uf028\\uf029 _t_ \\uf05d _T_ \\uf0b4 ------------\\uf0b6 _F_ **-** \\uf0b6 **a**<sup>_u_</sup> \\uf028\\uf029 _t u_ \\uf0ce _EUS_ \\uf028 _m_ \\uf029 EndFor _m_ EndFor _t_ Compute Gradients _Q_ \\uf0b6 _F T_ -------------------------- **-** = \\uf0e5 **d**<sup>_m_</sup> \\uf028\\uf029 _t_ \\uf0b4 \\uf05b **a**<sup>_l_</sup> \\uf028 _t_ – _d_ \\uf029\\uf05d \\uf0b6 **LW**<sup>_m_\\uf02c</sup><sup>_l_</sup> \\uf028\\uf029 _d t_ = 1 _Q_ \\uf0b6 _F T_ ------------------------ **-** = \\uf0e5 **d**<sup>_m_</sup> \\uf028\\uf029 _t_ \\uf0b4 \\uf05b **p**<sup>_l_</sup> \\uf028 _t_ – _d_ \\uf029\\uf05d \\uf0b6 **IW**<sup>_m_\\uf02c</sup><sup>_l_</sup> \\uf028\\uf029 _d t_ = 1 _Q_ \\uf0b6 _F_ ------- **-** = \\uf0e5 **d**<sup>_m_</sup> \\uf028\\uf029 _t_ \\uf0b6 **b**<sup>_m_</sup> _t_ = 1 \\n\\n**_<mark>14-35</mark>_** \\n\\n**_<mark>14 Dynamic Networks</mark>_** \\n\\n###### **Definitions/Notation** \\n\\n**p**<sup>_l_</sup> \\uf028\\uf029 _t_ is the _l_<sup>th</sup> _input vector_ to the network at time _t_ . \\n\\n**n**<sup>_m_</sup> \\uf028\\uf029 _t_ is the _net input_ for layer _m_ . \\n\\n**f**<sup>_m_</sup> \\uf028\\uf029 is the _transfer function_ for layer _m_ . \\n\\n**a**<sup>_m_</sup> \\uf028\\uf029 _t_ is the _output_ for layer _m_ . \\n\\n**IW**<sup>_m_\\uf02c</sup><sup>_l_</sup> is the _input weight_ between input _l_ and layer _m_ . \\n\\n**LW**<sup>_m_\\uf02c</sup><sup>_l_</sup> is the _layer weight_ between layer _l_ and layer _m_ . \\n\\n- **b**<sup>_m_</sup> is the _bias vector_ for layer _m_ . \\n\\n_DLm_ \\uf02c _l_ is the set of all delays in the tapped delay line between Layer _l_ and Layer _m._ \\n\\n_DIm_ \\uf02c _l_ is the set of all delays in the tapped delay line between Input _l_ and Layer _m_ . \\n\\n- _Im_ is the set of indices of input vectors that connect to layer _m_ . \\n\\n- _Lfm_ is the set of indices of layers that directly connect _forward_ to layer _m_ . \\n\\n_Lbm_ is the set of indices of layers that are directly connected backwards to layer _m_ (or to which layer _m_ connects forward) and that contain no delays in the connection. \\n\\nA layer is an _input layer_ if it has an input weight, or if it contains any delays with any of its weight matrices. The set of input layers is _X_ . \\n\\nA layer is an _output layer_ if its output will be compared to a target during training, or if it is connected to an input layer through a matrix that has any delays associated with it. The set of output layers is _U_ . \\n\\nThe _sensitivity_ is defined _suk_ \\uf02c\\uf02c _im_ \\uf028\\uf029 _t_ \\uf0ba ----------------\\uf0b6<sup>_e_</sup> _auk_ \\uf028\\uf029 _t_ . \\uf0b6 _nmi_ \\uf028\\uf029 _t EULW_ \\uf028\\uf029 _x_ = \\uf07b _u_ \\uf0ce _U_ \\uf027 \\uf024\\uf028 **LW**<sup>_x_</sup> \\uf02c<sup>_u_</sup> \\uf028\\uf029 _d_ \\uf0b9 0 \\uf02c _d_ \\uf0b9 0 \\uf029\\uf07d _EXS_ \\uf028\\uf029 _u_ = \\uf07b _x_ \\uf0ce _X_ \\uf027 \\uf024\\uf028 **S**<sup>_u_</sup> \\uf02c<sup>_x_</sup> \\uf0b9 0 \\uf029\\uf07d _ES_ \\uf028\\uf029 _u_ = \\uf07b _x_ \\uf027 \\uf024\\uf028 **S**<sup>_u_</sup> \\uf02c<sup>_x_</sup> \\uf0b9 0 \\uf029\\uf07d _EXLW_ \\uf028\\uf029 _u_ = \\uf07b _x_ \\uf0ce _X_ \\uf027 \\uf024\\uf028 **LW**<sup>_x_</sup> \\uf02c<sup>_u_</sup> \\uf028\\uf029 _d_ \\uf0b9 0 \\uf02c _d_ \\uf0b9 0 \\uf029\\uf07d _EUS_ \\uf028\\uf029 _x_ = \\uf07b _u_ \\uf0ce _U_ \\uf027 \\uf024\\uf028 **S**<sup>_u_</sup> \\uf02c<sup>_x_</sup> \\uf0b9 0 \\uf029\\uf07d \\n\\n**_<mark>14-36</mark>_** \\n\\n**_<mark>Solved Problems</mark>_** \\n\\n##### **Solved Problems** \\n\\n###### **P14.1 Before stating the problem, let’s first introduce some notation that will allow us to efficiently represent dynamic networks:** \\n\\nLayer #1 with 2 tansig neurons. Input vector with 3 elements. \\n\\n\\n\\n<!-- Start of picture text -->\\n1<br>2 3<br>Tapped delay from 1 to 9. Tapped delay from 0 to 9.<br>9